 "description": "PyJson.Loads models CPython 3.13's C recursion budget for every port, not only the stateless helpers (state consolidation; it used to model the container limit alone). With B = 9998 for json.loads called from Python code and n the open containers: a decode error built in C needs n <= B - 4; a Python object_pairs_hook or parse_constant needs two levels and a third to raise (margo_store.parse_json's duplicate-key and non-finite StateErrors); NaN through the default parse_constant, 'Expecting value' and the 4300-digit ValueError need one. work_state.py source reads parse_json, import-preview plain json.loads; each deep case has a control one level shallower.",
